                        "form": "сы́ростях"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "273d8d9e-be36-3fc0-ab82-3d4004d0bf5d",
                        "entry_id": "f6f8b625-6a9f-37c9-a000-09981b5d7c21",
                        "glosses": [
                            "свойство по значению прилагательного сырой"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3b1bd239-8a97-4e97-b8bc-d11a7bbd1fed",
                                "sense_id": "273d8d9e-be36-3fc0-ab82-3d4004d0bf5d",
                                "text": "Тот, бывало, как увидит, что около него нечисто, — сейчас задней ногой стук в стенку стойла; а этому ничего — хоть по самое брюхо навали ему навозу. Тот, если, например, против ветра его поставить, — сейчас всеми лёгкими вздохнёт и встряхнётся, а этот знай пофыркивает; того сырость дождевая беспокоила — этому она нипочём…"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4b059504-2eae-326f-9f92-6775db263092",
                        "entry_id": "f6f8b625-6a9f-37c9-a000-09981b5d7c21",
                        "glosses": [
                            "большое содержание влаги в чём-либо"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "76afa6cf-702d-45f9-a85a-1350afca67b0",
                                "sense_id": "4b059504-2eae-326f-9f92-6775db263092",
                                "text": "Уже не ожесточение испытывал он, а ту особенную одеревенелость чувства, которая, говорят, овладевает человеком перед совершением преступления. Но собственный голос испугал его — так дико прозвучал он под навесом тёмных ветвей, в гнилой и спёртой сырости лесного оврага!"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2e0a0a39-96f0-41ca-9121-021a89023f96",
                        "source_entry_id": "f6f8b625-6a9f-37c9-a000-09981b5d7c21",
                        "target_lang_word": "wetness",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "wetness",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cfc06c22-37af-3085-bf18-1a999a7b49a8",
                                        "entry_id": "fb704ba9-bfc8-36f2-a4af-bb06dca5f449",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The condition of being wet."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c749ae67-863a-4ef2-93c2-bf249b00be22",
                                                "sense_id": "cfc06c22-37af-3085-bf18-1a999a7b49a8",
                                                "text": "The young man looked long and fixedly on the place, the sight of which interested him so much that he had forgotten, in the eagerness of youthful curiosity, the wetness of his dress."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "50f2ca2f-35bd-4875-b94b-1d0abf991e34",
                                                "sense_id": "cfc06c22-37af-3085-bf18-1a999a7b49a8",
                                                "text": "The first business was to make a fire, an operation which was a little delayed by the wetness of the fuel and the ground, owing to the heavy showers of the afternoon."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c213ad8b-8a09-4c44-896d-dcb5aecde5ab",
                                                "sense_id": "cfc06c22-37af-3085-bf18-1a999a7b49a8",
                                                "text": "The industrial brewers continue to prosper, but now they are facing a new challenge from local brewers across the country who are dedicated to turning out brews that have only one thing in common with industrial beer—wetness."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bb69c57c-ab33-3089-9bd7-c24f4f10b6b5",
                                        "entry_id": "fb704ba9-bfc8-36f2-a4af-bb06dca5f449",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Moisture."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3b1954c6-4e19-4de1-ba56-e08308c3f2c8",
                                                "sense_id": "bb69c57c-ab33-3089-9bd7-c24f4f10b6b5",
                                                "text": "“Oh! if I had my gravity,” thought she, contemplating the water, “I would flash off this balcony like a long white sea-bird, headlong into the darling wetness. Heigh-ho!”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d87c06b4-61b1-484e-858b-3e100ea08912",
                                                "sense_id": "bb69c57c-ab33-3089-9bd7-c24f4f10b6b5",
                                                "text": "And so nature was not interfered with in the middle of the rainy season. Sometimes it poured down in such thick sheets of water that earth and sky seemed merged in one grey wetness."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1601032e-c0e1-328a-a952-a2cdd24de988",
                                        "entry_id": "fb704ba9-bfc8-36f2-a4af-bb06dca5f449",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Rainy or damp weather."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2a8bd2b3-afb1-4f10-bed1-445d65d95d61",
                                                "sense_id": "1601032e-c0e1-328a-a952-a2cdd24de988",
                                                "text": "1797, Tobias Smollett et al., The History of England, from the Revolution to the End of the American War and the Peace of Versailles in 1783, Philadelphia: Robert Campbell, Volume 4, Book 5, p. 484,\nThey complained, that the wetness of the season, and the scarcity of fodder in the year 1762, with other natural causes, had reduced the quantity of fat cattle, by discouraging the farmers from rearing them."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "badf37e3-6f79-4fde-9997-468f3e32b303",
                                                "sense_id": "1601032e-c0e1-328a-a952-a2cdd24de988",
                                                "text": "Tanoo, Skedans and Cumshewa lie fairly close to each other on the map, yet each is quite unlike the others when you come to it. All have the West Coast wetness but Cumshewa seems always to drip, always to be blurred with mist, its foliage always to hang wet-heavy."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7705ca4f-412a-40de-b437-d70c77f61344",
                        "source_entry_id": "f6f8b625-6a9f-37c9-a000-09981b5d7c21",
                        "target_lang_word": "Feuchtigkeit",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Feuchtigkeit",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4b8c78e9-a848-3250-a5e8-f50783310322",
                                        "entry_id": "d0e5cbc2-9b5d-3856-950a-5237a981b7ae",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Zustand, feucht zu sein; Vorhandensein von Wasser (oder anderen Flüssigkeiten) in geringen Mengen"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2309f944-0c32-46ac-b3e1-0ebcc8955f1d",
                                                "sense_id": "4b8c78e9-a848-3250-a5e8-f50783310322",
                                                "text": "Die Feuchtigkeit in den Zimmerwänden kann zur Schimmelbildung führen."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "80809574-c141-4eaf-a92b-e5c622616722",
                                                "sense_id": "4b8c78e9-a848-3250-a5e8-f50783310322",
                                                "text": "Bei Feuchtigkeit auf dem Boden kann man leicht darauf/darin ausrutschen."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f59c69b3-4ede-47cb-b2b9-815ba914fb4e",
                                                "sense_id": "4b8c78e9-a848-3250-a5e8-f50783310322",
                                                "text": "„Neben Feuchtigkeit und Luftverschmutzung haben Mikroorganismen einen bedeutenden Anteil am Zerfall alter Wandgemälde.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3278fb23-9f20-438c-a0dd-4cbb8371b873",
                                                "sense_id": "4b8c78e9-a848-3250-a5e8-f50783310322",
                                                "text": "„Die Feuchtigkeit des Holzes drang durch die Hosen.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "df05250e-2081-4d48-b364-aacedb5168dd",
                                                "sense_id": "4b8c78e9-a848-3250-a5e8-f50783310322",
                                                "text": "„Es taut heftig, die Wiese wird feucht, aber auch die Feuchtigkeit können die Menschen hier vertragen, daran sind sie von Jugend auf gewöhnt.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "872d966e-c044-485f-a7b7-0bbdeef4042e",
                                                "sense_id": "4b8c78e9-a848-3250-a5e8-f50783310322",
                                                "text": "„Es sah so aus, als sei Feuchtigkeit in der Luft.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
